  "notes": "Barracora gameplay causality with direct public switch writes only (keyboard handling and the driver's simulator stay off). Three balls rest on ball ramp switches 13, 14 and 15; a coin and the credit button start a game, which must throw a ball (solenoid 12) towards the shooter (switch 16), and the upper eject hole gate (17) must energize after the plunge. The jet bumper and kicker scoring switches 20, 21, 22, 29 and 30 must each publish their switch-driven special solenoid 18-22 at once. A top lane and the synthetic flipper buttons 82 and 84 show outputs 45-48 and the lane-change copies 35 and 34. The drop banks are worked out of and in sequence with targets held down until the ROM resets them (real drop targets stay down), the lit eject holes lock two balls for 3-ball Multi-Ball, one ball drains into the outhole, and a single ball roll tilt closure must drop game-on 25. The host moves balls between ramp positions itself; that movement is not ROM evidence. Run from an NVRAM initialized by one prior empty-NVRAM power-up.",
